    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "11. Charge Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "11.04",
    "order": 154,
    "anchor": "11.04",
    "summary": "A unit that has **declared a charge** in this phase can move up to its **charge roll**, following the [Moving rules](vsdata:core-rule/moving) (03):\n\n1. Before moving, pick 1 or more enemy units within 12\" and within that distance; each is a charge target until the move ends.\n2. While moving, each model must end closer to at least 1 charge target and, where it can, within 1\" of one and **engaged** with one.\n3. After moving, the unit has to be [engaged](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) with every charge target and with no other enemy unit, and its models have **[Fights First](vsdata:core-ability/fights-first)** until the turn ends.",
